# UI/UX Governance (Framework-Independent)

**Scope:** Presentation principles that apply regardless of React, Vue, or future adapters.  
**Contracts:** `UI-CONTRACT.md`, `PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md`  
**Implementation rules:** `react-inertia.mdc` (React + Inertia stack only)

```text
02-ui-ux.mdc        → UX principles, states, a11y, design system intent
react-inertia.mdc   → React 19 + Inertia 3 + Tailwind 4 implementation details
```

## Component-First

```text
Page → Layout → Toolbar → Form/Grid → Dialog → Actions
```

Search existing components before creating new ones.

## Required UI States

Every async UI: `idle`, `loading`, `success`, `empty`, `error`, `disabled`, `retry`.

## Design System

```text
CSS variables (--sis-*) → Tailwind → shared components → pages
```

No random colors/spacing. Tailwind is styling tool — not architecture.

## Forms

- Client validation = UX only; server validation is authoritative
- Labels, focus, keyboard, touch targets (min ~44px mobile)
- Form wiring (`useForm`, routes) → see `react-inertia.mdc`

## Grids

Server pagination always. Mobile: cards/stack — not forced desktop tables.

## Accessibility

Keyboard nav, focus management, semantic HTML, ARIA where needed, contrast.

## RTL

Arabic RTL first-class — layout and interaction principles here; Tailwind/logical properties and i18n wiring in `react-inertia.mdc`.

## Automatic Optimization

Every UI change MUST pass optimization evaluation automatically — see `15-ui-optimization-governance.mdc` and `UI-OPTIMIZATION-GOVERNANCE.md`. Not optional; not a separate phase.

## No Business Logic in UI

Authorization checks in UI are **indicators only**. Never duplicate enrollment/eligibility/tenant rules in React.
